                "{\"score\":6,\"reasoning\":\"All four expected panels are present and readable, and the six Q histograms show a clear shift toward lower Q with increasing temperature. The bead chain is connected but elongated rather than compact, with several projected crossings and no depth cues to assess geometry. Heat capacity varies with temperature, but its maximum occurs at the lowest sampled temperature, not at the reported transition T*=0.657. The free-energy profile has a plausible central basin but no resolved folding barrier or competing basins; its flat tails look artificially capped, and the transition assignment is not convincingly supported. It is smoother than the reference's severely spiked free-energy curve, but scientific consistency remains limited.\"}"
